; link/pop_flames.link — the torch-flame code bundle (P3.17 phase B).
;
; A SEPARATE IMAGE, loaded from a raw track at run time rather than carried inside
; the program. The reason is the one link/pop_engine.link already documents: a
; LOADM'd engine must stay under $25FF, because above that is BASIC's program and
; variable area — DECB's own workspace — and a load that runs through it clobbers
; the loader. Nine compiled flames are ~3.1 KB, which puts the program at $2C5A and
; breaks LOADM outright (measured: no "OK" after the command, second segment absent).
;
; $0A00 is the intro's asset-bundle region, and it is used the same way here: the
; room reads one track into it and indexes the pointer tables at the head.
;
;   $3000-$3035   three 9-entry dispatch tables (draw / save / erase)
;   $3036-$3039   char_tab (retired, reserved so the offsets below hold)
;   $303A-$303F   blit_tab   (blit_cel / blit_save / blit_erase)
;   $3040-$3041   chars_tab  (chars_frame)
;   $3042-...     the compiled cels, the baked character cels, the blitter,
;                 char_draw, and the VM's cel table
;
; TWO TRACKS from P3.25, following the intro bundle's worked precedent
; (intro_seq.s:140-159: DISK_BUNDLE_TRK 25 "two tracks", BUNDLE $3000 = 9,216 B ->
; $52FF, SAVE_BUF $5400 sited clear of it).
;
; IT COULD NOT GROW IN PLACE. At the old base, two tracks reach $0A00+9,216 = $2E00
; and ROOM.BIN's prog starts at $2000 -- the bundle would have loaded straight over
; the engine. $4200 sat immediately after the room blob ($3000..$41FF).
;
; $4200 -> $3000 AT P3.31, ONTO THE ROOM BLOB'S GROUND. The walk's twelve cels take the
; bundle to 14,258 B, and from $4200 the contiguous room below the disk driver's
; parameter block at $6A00 is 10,240 -- it does not fit at all. The blob at $3000 is
; 4,608 B and is DEAD once the room is drawn (one expand, and since P3.22 the second
; buffer is filled by HAL_gfx_mirror rather than a second expand), so the bundle lives
; there instead: $3000-$67B2 unpacked, still clear of $6A00, of the peel buffers at
; $6C00, of the trace ring at $7800 and of the kernel at $7900. It ARRIVES packed --
; see cutscene_room.s bundle_expand for why nothing else fits through load_tracks.
;
; THIS ADDRESS IS THE ONE COPY THE ASSEMBLER CANNOT SEE. The two .s files take
; FLAME_BASE from build.bat's -D; the linker cannot read that, so it is repeated here,
; and decb_to_raw refuses an image whose first segment is not exactly at the base
; build.bat states -- which is what turns a drift between these two into a build error.
;
; Nothing else may live at $3000 while the room is running. The intro's bundle uses
; the same region, but the two programs never run at once.

section prog load 3000

entry torch0_cels
